# A building `match` with no arm, over a choice with no case (Semantics ch. 4, "The
# widget block": a building `match` over a plain scrutinee; hosting attempt 29 and its
# ruling: a `match` with no arm over an empty choice is legal). No value of `Never`
# exists, so the line builds nothing and the block that holds it is never built; the
# program around it builds as if the line were not there.
# Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@Absurd: fn Never -> @unit
fn @Absurd never:
    Ui.Label($text=$"no value reaches this")
    match never:

@Slot: fn ?Never -> @unit
fn @Slot ?never:
    Ui.Label($text=$"before")                                    # 0
    match ?never:
        ? never: @Absurd never
        nil: Ui.Label($text=$"nothing asked")                    # 1
    Ui.Label($text=$"after")                                     # 2
